# Bankrupt in Blood: the additional cost (sacrifice two creatures) is paid as the spell is cast (CR 601.2h), so a spell
# countered on the stack has already cost both creatures, and "Draw three cards" never happens (CR 608.2: only a
# resolving spell follows its instructions). Bot2 counters it with Counterspell (an Island and Mox Sapphire).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Bankrupt in Blood
Swamp x2
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bankrupt in Blood.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter; Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Bankrupt in Blood)
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Bankrupt in Blood; Ornithopter; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
